<para><anchor id="EXAMPLES_DRIVERS_ADC_EX3_TEMPERATURE_SENSOR_1md__home_siddharth_ti_repos_c29_sdk_docs_docs_src_docs_api_guide_examples_drivers_adc_ex3_temperature_sensor"/></para>
<sect1 id="EXAMPLES_DRIVERS_ADC_EX3_TEMPERATURE_SENSOR_1autotoc_md135">
<title>Introduction</title>
<para>This example sets up the ePWM (MCPWM in case of F28E12x and MCPC029) to periodically trigger the ADC. The ADC converts the internal connection to the temperature sensor, which is then interpreted as a temperature by calling the <ref refid="group__adc__api_1ga8a5cb219b8d081574e4434d4e7329204" kindref="member">ADC_getTemperatureC()</ref> function.</para>
<para>Watch Variables<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>sensorSample - The raw reading from the temperature sensor</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>sensorTemp - The interpretation of the sensor sample as a temperature in degrees Celsius.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="EXAMPLES_DRIVERS_ADC_EX3_TEMPERATURE_SENSOR_1autotoc_md136">
<title>External Connections</title>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>None.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
